  "turn_number": 4,
  "player_text": "I glance toward the crowded gate, then back at the captain. \"Whose orders are you waiting on, and do you think they want this left alone? If I'm walking out to that milestone, I want to know what I'm walking into.\"",
  "visible_motivation": "The captain says higher-up orders have held back a search, and travelers last saw the patrol heading toward an old milestone northwest.",
  "intended_meaning": "I want to know who is delaying the search and whether the milestone lead is safe to follow.",
  "generation_attempt_1": "The guard captain glances briefly toward the cluster of gate guards and serjeants around the crowded gate. \"We're waiting on orders from the city watch commander,\" they say quietly, voice low as if wary of nearby ears. \"No official word yet on whether to investigate the missing patrol or to let the matter rest for now.\"\n\nThe captain's narrowed eyes flick toward the notice board listing the missing patrol warning. \"If you're heading out to that milestone,\" they add carefully, \"be ready for whatever. No one knows for sure what happened, and the brass seems hesitant to stir the hornet's nest.\"",
